# Example ReRDMFT input file: Ne, cc-pVDZ, X2C, FUNCTIONAL PCCD, FULL_OPTIMIZATION.
# CHOLESKY TRUE: X2C's 2*n_spatial = 30-dimensional spinor problem is cheap either way, but this
# matches the C4_DHF companion example (ne_pccd_c4.inp), where it matters more.
#
# X2C-HF uses the renormalized X2C-1e core (X2C_NORM TRUE) and ordinary non-relativistic two-electron
# integrals (no two-electron picture change): X2C-HF -128.6328725 Hartree (PySCF spinor X2C-1e: same),
# FULL_OPTIMIZATION -128.7019321 Hartree, 1.1 mHartree below the exact 4-component value of
# ne_pccd_c4.inp (-128.7008622 Hartree).
NELEC 10
BASIS ne-cc-pvdz.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
X2C TRUE
FUNCTIONAL PCCD
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
CHOLESKY TRUE
ON_DEMAND_ERI FALSE  # off here to keep this example's historical fast runtime (the whole packed AO tensor already fits in memory); default is TRUE, see lih_gnof_c4_full_optimization_cholesky.inp for the on-demand path demonstrated explicitly.

GEOMETRY
Ne  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
END
